From f8c76e358b998764731509e1ce8b13b0feb75dfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 19:52:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: the About tile stranded a strip of empty rail at the
 bottom of a page

.railabout is position:sticky with bottom:14px, but .rail carried
padding:14px 12px 56px. A sticky element is constrained to its containing
block's CONTENT box, which that 56px shrinks - so the tile rode 14px above the
viewport floor for the whole scroll, then released at the end of a long page and
settled 56px up, revealing 42px of bare rail underneath it.

Bottom padding is now 14px, equal to the sticky offset, so the resting position
and the riding position are the same and there is nothing to reveal. Both chrome
pages move together, per the standing rule.

The old comment justified the 56px as clearance from the browser's URL/status
tooltip. That was already defeated - the sticky tile rides at 14px for the whole
scroll, so the clearance only ever existed on the last screen of a page, which is
exactly where it showed up as a gap. Comment rewritten to say so, and both files
now state that the two numbers must move together.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp | 10 +++++++++-
 release/src/router/www/reaper_shell.asp    | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp b/release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp
index 79afeb9d82..c7ee243efa 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp
@@ -86,7 +86,15 @@ html{scrollbar-width:thin;scrollbar-color:var(--crimson) #000}
    min-content width and the whole document overflows to the right */
 main{min-width:0}
 .rail{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#0c0c0f,#08080a);border-right:1px solid var(--line-soft);
-  display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:14px 12px 56px;gap:2px}
+  /* reaper 2026-08-25 (field): this bottom padding MUST stay equal to
+     .railabout's sticky `bottom` offset below (14px). The About tile is
+     position:sticky, so while you scroll it rides 14px above the viewport
+     floor, and at the END of a long page sticky releases and it settles at
+     its flow position - the rail's content-box bottom. At 56px that landing
+     spot was 42px higher than where the tile had been riding, so hitting the
+     bottom of a page dropped an empty strip of rail underneath it. Keep the
+     two numbers in step or the strip comes back. */
+  display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:14px 12px 14px;gap:2px}
 .railclock{padding:6px 6px 14px;text-align:center;line-height:1.05}
 .railclock .rc-time{font-family:var(--hdr);font-weight:700;font-size:23px;letter-spacing:.07em;color:var(--bone);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
 .railclock .rc-sec{color:var(--crimson)}
diff --git a/release/src/router/www/reaper_shell.asp b/release/src/router/www/reaper_shell.asp
index 3b97a6c9a6..43743fd746 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/reaper_shell.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/reaper_shell.asp
@@ -82,10 +82,22 @@ html{scrollbar-width:thin;scrollbar-color:var(--crimson) #000}
 /* rail: no scrollbar of its own - the page scrollbar handles overflow */
 /* rail is locked to the page: NO scrollbar of its own - it scrolls with the
    body so the only page scrollbar is the one on the far right (the framed
-   iframe keeps its own internal scrollbar, which is fine). padding-bottom gives
-   the last item breathing room from the browser URL/status tooltip. */
+   iframe keeps its own internal scrollbar, which is fine). padding-bottom is
+   NOT free to pick - see the note on .rail below; it is pinned to the About
+   tile's sticky offset. It used to be 56px for clearance from the browser's
+   URL/status tooltip, but the sticky tile already rides at 14px for the whole
+   scroll, so that clearance only ever existed on the last screen of a page -
+   which is exactly where it showed up as a gap instead. */
 .rail{grid-column:1;grid-row:1 / 3;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#0c0c0f,#08080a);border-right:1px solid var(--line-soft);
-  display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:14px 12px 56px;gap:2px}
+  /* reaper 2026-08-25 (field): this bottom padding MUST stay equal to
+     .railabout's sticky `bottom` offset below (14px). The About tile is
+     position:sticky, so while you scroll it rides 14px above the viewport
+     floor, and at the END of a long page sticky releases and it settles at
+     its flow position - the rail's content-box bottom. At 56px that landing
+     spot was 42px higher than where the tile had been riding, so hitting the
+     bottom of a page dropped an empty strip of rail underneath it. Keep the
+     two numbers in step or the strip comes back. */
+  display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:14px 12px 14px;gap:2px}
 .railclock{padding:6px 6px 14px;text-align:center;line-height:1.05}
 .railclock .rc-time{font-family:var(--hdr);font-weight:700;font-size:23px;letter-spacing:.07em;color:var(--bone);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
 .railclock .rc-sec{color:var(--crimson)}
